From: Banana <bananalinux@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] audio/common/alsa: fall back to a working buffer when a core asks for too much

A core may ask for more latency than the device's frontend can hold at all: the
PlayStation cores request 192 ms unconditionally through
RETRO_ENVIRONMENT_SET_MINIMUM_AUDIO_LATENCY, and the audioreach frontend on the
Retroid Pocket Classic refuses it -- and, following it, the periods request and
then snd_pcm_hw_params() itself, so RetroArch tore the driver down and carried on
without audio: PSX games were silent while every other core (which asks for
nothing) played.

When the requested buffer is refused, ask again for Banana's own 64 ms (the shape
every working stream on this handheld uses; or the user's setting if it is even
smaller -- the core has already overwritten audio_latency with its own request, so
that value cannot be trusted), and treat a refused period count as a warning
rather than fatal: snd_pcm_hw_params() then picks one the frontend supports. The
failure message also stops reporting a stale errnum where it meant the call's own
result.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/audio/common/alsa.c
+++ b/audio/common/alsa.c
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@
 
 #include "../audio_driver.h"
 #include "../../verbosity.h"
+#include "../../configuration.h"
 
 int alsa_init_pcm(snd_pcm_t **pcm,
    const char* device,
@@ -141,27 +142,49 @@
    if (new_rate)
       *new_rate = rate;
 
-   if ((snd_pcm_hw_params_set_buffer_time_near(*pcm, params, &latency_usec, NULL)) < 0)
-   {
-      RARCH_ERR("[ALSA] Failed to request a buffer time near %uus for %s device \"%s\": %s.\n",
-            latency_usec,
-            snd_pcm_stream_name(stream),
-            snd_pcm_name(*pcm),
-            snd_strerror(errnum));
-
-      goto error;
-
+   /*
+    * A core can ask for more latency than the device's frontend can hold at all: the PlayStation cores ask
+    * for 192 ms unconditionally through RETRO_ENVIRONMENT_SET_MINIMUM_AUDIO_LATENCY, and the audioreach
+    * frontend on the Retroid Pocket Classic refuses it -- and, following it, the periods request too, so
+    * the whole audio driver comes up dead and the game runs in silence. Failing here is not graceful
+    * either: the caller carries on with a handle it never finished configuring and asserts on
+    * snd_pcm_avail() a few frames later (a crash, and a game that never appears). So when the requested
+    * buffer is refused, ask for the size every working stream on this handheld uses -- the user's own
+    * configured latency if it is smaller, otherwise 64 ms.
+    */
+   if ((errnum = snd_pcm_hw_params_set_buffer_time_near(*pcm, params, &latency_usec, NULL)) < 0)
+   {
+      settings_t *settings     = config_get_ptr();
+      unsigned fallback_us     = 64000u;
+      /* The core has already raised audio_latency to its own request, so the setting can be the very value
+       * the device just refused: ask for Banana's own 64 ms instead (every working stream on this handheld
+       * uses it), unless the user asked for even less. */
+      if (settings && settings->uints.audio_latency > 0
+            && settings->uints.audio_latency < 64)
+         fallback_us = settings->uints.audio_latency * 1000u;
+
+      RARCH_WARN("[ALSA] %s device \"%s\" will not take a %ums buffer (%s).\n",
+            snd_pcm_stream_name(stream), snd_pcm_name(*pcm), latency_usec / 1000u,
+            snd_strerror(errnum));
+
+      latency_usec = fallback_us;
+      errnum       = snd_pcm_hw_params_set_buffer_time_near(*pcm, params, &latency_usec, NULL);
+      if (errnum == 0)
+         RARCH_WARN("[ALSA] Using a %ums buffer instead.\n", latency_usec / 1000u);
+      else
+      {
+         RARCH_WARN("[ALSA] Leaving the buffer size to the device.\n");
+         errnum = 0;	/* no buffer asked for at all: snd_pcm_hw_params() picks what it supports */
+      }
    }
 
    if ((errnum = snd_pcm_hw_params_set_periods_near(*pcm, params, &periods, NULL)) < 0)
    {
-      RARCH_ERR("[ALSA] Failed to request %u periods per buffer for %s device \"%s\": %s.\n",
-            periods,
-            snd_pcm_stream_name(stream),
-            snd_pcm_name(*pcm),
-            snd_strerror(errnum));
-
-      goto error;
+      /* A period count the frontend refuses does not make the stream unusable: the buffer time above is
+       * what the amplifiers care about, and snd_pcm_hw_params() below picks a period count it supports. */
+      RARCH_WARN("[ALSA] %s device \"%s\" will not take %u periods (%s); letting it choose.\n",
+            snd_pcm_stream_name(stream), snd_pcm_name(*pcm), periods, snd_strerror(errnum));
+      errnum = 0;
    }
 
    if ((errnum = snd_pcm_hw_params(*pcm, params)) < 0)
